    "kanji/滝.md": {
      "added": [
        "酒"
      ],
      "meaningBefore": "[滝](../words/滝.md) たき is a waterfall. The complete word family also records rapids, marked archaic in JMdict; the monolingual sources likewise distinguish older fast-current use from the usual modern waterfall focus. 日本国語大辞典 additionally records an abbreviation of 滝水, water from a waterfall.",
      "meaningAfter": "[滝](../words/滝.md) たき is a waterfall. The complete word family also records rapids, marked archaic in JMdict; the monolingual sources likewise distinguish older fast-current use from the usual modern waterfall focus. 日本国語大辞典 additionally records 滝 as an Edo-period abbreviation of 滝水 たきすい, the name of a sake sold in Edo; that historical sense is not taught here.",
      "liquidNote": "- [液](液.md) receives a qualified precaution for the broad liquid/fluid label: 滝 is a flow of water, 字通 also records soaking/moistening, and 日本国語大辞典's abbreviated sense names a drink. デジタル大辞泉 defines 液 as a formless flowing substance such as water or oil. Not every liquid is a waterfall, and 滝 is not taught as meaning liquid generally.",
      "sakeNote": "- [酒](酒.md) receives a qualified precaution for its alcohol/sake label. 日本国語大辞典 records 滝 as short for 滝水 たきすい, a named sake sold by a shop in Edo's Kanda; the waterfall-water words 滝水 たきみず and ろうすい are separate readings. This historical abbreviation is not a modern sense of 滝, and 滝 is not taught as meaning alcohol.",
      "insertedMetadata": [
        "Abbreviated sense: 日本国語大辞典's",
        "[滝水](https://kotobank.jp/word/滝水), たきすい."
      ],
